From: Jacques Germishuys <jacques.germishuys@bloudraad.io>
Subject: [PATCH] fix: release completed DMA before completing requests

The deferred callback reference can keep a completed transaction alive.
Release its DMA buffer references before completing the send request to
prevent KMDF bugcheck 0x10D/3 after Windows 7 restore.

Signed-off-by: Jacques Germishuys <jacques.germishuys@bloudraad.io>
---
diff --git a/VirtIO/WDF/Dma.c b/VirtIO/WDF/Dma.c
index 17bc4bb..1024031 100644
--- a/VirtIO/WDF/Dma.c
+++ b/VirtIO/WDF/Dma.c
@@ -388,5 +388,6 @@ void VirtIOWdfDeviceDmaTxComplete(VirtIODevice *vdev, WDFDMATRANSACTION transact
     NTSTATUS status;
     DPrintf(1, "%s %p\n", __FUNCTION__, transaction);
     WdfDmaTransactionDmaCompletedFinal(transaction, 0, &status);
+    WdfDmaTransactionRelease(transaction);
     DerefTransaction(ctx);
 }
